    "joint corner points are measured (corner lib + .temp in one ngspice run); the 48 mismatch draws were measured at TT/27 C only and are applied as per-chip RELATIVE factors (declared composition, not a re-run of MC at each corner)",
    "full calibration is the continuous-trim upper bound (100 ppm floor); the real gm/leak code range is a B3 characterization item, so 'full' brackets the loop, it does not measure it",
    "no_track/bg_track model the loop at test (per-chip, 27 C): the process corner is trimmed at test, so only the temperature excursion remains; bg refresh granularity 1 C is DECLARED",
    "poisson-2d is compiled on the 8x8 mesh (64 states) in this lane: compose.run_chain's Lyapunov/mask cost scales ~n^3 and the 16x16 anchor measured >10 min here. The property under test (the DC solution is set by conductance RATIOS, so a uniform corner scale cancels) is grid-independent; the QoI uses the declared 1 ns MODEL-time deadline mapped through P3 to alpha*1 ns = 237 tau_phys (steady state, not the pre-relaxation b*T regime); the 16x16 anchor remains the run_pipeline workload",
    "the step-response QoI is a conservative proxy for the operator error seen by the workload, not a re-run of the nonlinear PDE",
    "the 100 ppm calibration floor is applied uniformly to diag/gm/edges; the measured QoI error under 'full' is ~1e-4 (diffusion 9.995e-5, burgers 9.12e-5) and ratio-cancelled for poisson (9.8e-16). No growth amplification is observed in this lane: the earlier ~4% claim came from perturbing a single axis, not the uniform coefficient scale",
